
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-4 pb-5 privacy-content">

    <h1 class="mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="text-muted mb-4">
        Last updated: 29 September 2026
    </p>

    <p class="lead">
        Your privacy is important to us.
    </p>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Mart Ops collects, uses,
        stores and protects personal information when you visit our
        website, register for an account or use our associated
        web and mobile applications.
    </p>

    <p>
        Mart Ops is a glazing operations management platform,
        currently provided as a demonstration system for
        technical evaluation and general interest.
    </p>

    

    <h4 class="mt-4">1. Who we are</h4>

    <p>
        Mart Ops is developed and operated by Craig Griffiths,
        based in Greater Manchester, United Kingdom.
    </p>

    <p>
        For privacy enquiries, please contact:
        <a href="mailto:contact@glassops.co.uk">
            contact@glassops.co.uk
        </a>.
    </p>

    <p>
        Where we determine how and why personal information is
        processed, we act as the data controller.
        Where an organisation uses Mart Ops to manage its own
        customer or job information, that organisation may be
        the data controller and Mart Ops may act as its
        data processor.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">2. Information we collect</h4>

    <p>
        Depending on how you use Mart Ops, the following
        types of information may be collected and processed.
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-3">Account and company information</h5>

    <ul>
        <li>Name and contact details</li>
        <li>Email address and account credentials</li>
        <li>Company name and branch information</li>
        <li>User roles and account permissions</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="mt-3">Customer and job information</h5>

    <ul>
        <li>Customer names, addresses and contact details</li>
        <li>Contract and appointment information</li>
        <li>Insurance claim and policy information</li>
        <li>Survey, fitting and remedial work records</li>
        <li>Photographs, videos, drawings and signatures</li>
        <li>Job notes and associated documentation</li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="mt-3">Technical information</h5>

    <p>
        Technical information may be collected as part of
        operating and securing the website and applications.
        This may include IP addresses, browser information,
        authentication events and diagnostic information.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">3. How we use your information</h4>

    <p>
        Personal information is processed for purposes
        associated with operating and maintaining
        Mart Ops, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Creating and managing user accounts</li>
        <li>Providing access to authorised users</li>
        <li>Managing contracts, appointments and job records</li>
        <li>Supporting surveying and fitting operations</li>
        <li>Providing customer and insurer portal functionality</li>
        <li>Responding to enquiries and technical support requests</li>
        <li>Maintaining system security and reliability</li>
        <li>Meeting applicable legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        We do not sell personal information to third parties.
    </p>

    @*
        Before publication:
        Add the verified lawful basis for each processing
        purpose. These may include contract, legal obligation,
        legitimate interests or consent, as appropriate.
        Do not publish an unverified lawful-basis statement.
    *@

    <h4 class="mt-4">4. Demonstration accounts</h4>

    <p>
        Mart Ops is currently available as a demonstration
        system. Demonstration accounts are intended for
        evaluating the platform and exploring its features.
    </p>

    <p>
        Users should avoid entering genuine customer information,
        confidential business information or sensitive personal
        information into demonstration accounts unless explicitly
        authorised to do so.
    </p>

    <p>
        Demonstration information may be reset or removed as
        part of development, maintenance or testing.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">5. Data security</h4>

    <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational
        measures to protect personal information against
        unauthorised access, alteration, loss and disclosure.
    </p>

    <p>
        These measures include access controls and
        authentication mechanisms intended to restrict
        access to authorised users.
    </p>

    <p>
        No internet-based service can guarantee absolute
        security. Users are encouraged to use strong,
        unique passwords and keep their login details
        confidential.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">6. Sharing information</h4>

    <p>
        Information entered into Mart Ops may be accessible
        to authorised users of the relevant organisation
        according to their assigned roles and permissions.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information may also be processed by third-party
        service providers involved in operating the platform,
        such as website hosting and infrastructure providers.
    </p>

    <p>
        Personal information may be disclosed where required
        by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">7. Data retention</h4>

    <p>
        Personal information is retained only for as long as
        necessary for the purposes for which it was collected,
        subject to applicable legal, contractual and operational
        requirements.
    </p>

    <p>
        Retention periods may vary depending on the type of
        information and the purpose for which it is processed.
        Where an organisation manages its own records through
        Mart Ops, its own retention policies may apply.
    </p>

    <p>
        To enquire about how long your information is kept,
        please contact us using the details below.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">8. Your privacy rights</h4>

    <p>
        Under UK data protection law, you may have the
        following rights, depending on the circumstances
        and the lawful basis for processing:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>To request access to your personal information</li>
        <li>To request correction of inaccurate information</li>
        <li>To request deletion of your information</li>
        <li>To request restriction of processing</li>
        <li>To object to certain types of processing</li>
        <li>To request data portability, where applicable</li>
        <li>To withdraw consent where processing relies on it</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You can contact us to make a request or ask questions
        about how your information is handled.
    </p>

    <p>
        If your information was entered by a glazing company,
        insurer or another organisation using Mart Ops,
        you may also need to contact that organisation
        directly, as it may be responsible for determining
        how your information is processed.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">9. Cookies</h4>

    <p>
        Mart Ops uses cookies to support website
        functionality, authentication and security.
    </p>

    <p>
        Essential cookies help the website operate correctly,
        including maintaining login sessions and protecting
        against certain security threats.
    </p>

    <p>
        The website also uses a cookie to remember your
        cookie preferences.
    </p>

    <p>
        Optional cookies, where used, are subject to the
        applicable consent requirements. You can review
        or change your cookie preferences using the
        Cookie settings option in the website footer.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">10. Third-party services</h4>

    <p>
        Mart Ops may contain links to third-party websites
        and services. These websites operate independently
        and have their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <p>
        We encourage you to review the privacy policies
        of any external websites you visit.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">11. Changes to this policy</h4>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be updated to reflect
        changes to Mart Ops, its functionality or
        applicable legal requirements.
    </p>

    <p>
        The date at the top of this page indicates
        when the policy was last updated.
    </p>

    <h4 class="mt-4">12. Contact and complaints</h4>

    <p>
        If you have any questions, concerns or requests
        relating to your personal information, please contact:
    </p>

    <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 my-3">
        <strong>Mart Ops</strong><br />
        Craig Griffiths<br />
        Greater Manchester, United Kingdom<br />
        Email:
        <a href="mailto:contact@glassops.co.uk">
            contact@glassops.co.uk
        </a>
    </div>

    <p>
        You also have the right to raise a complaint with
        the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO),
        the UK's independent data protection authority.
    </p>

    <p>
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Visit the ICO website
        </a>
    </p>

    

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between
                align-items-center flex-wrap gap-3">

        <span class="text-muted small">
            Last updated: 29 September 2026
        </span>

        <a asp-area=""
           asp-controller="Home"
           asp-action="Index"
           class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            Back to Home
        </a>

    </div>

</div>
